{"name":"Chinchilla","hex":"#9c8e7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chinchilla","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Chinchillidae – the chinchillas."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Spanish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chinchilla"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chinchilla","blocks":[{"text":"Chinchilla is a genus consisting of two species of crepuscular rodents of the parvorder Caviomorpha, native to the Andes Mountains in South America. They live in colonies called \"herds\" at high elevations up to 4,270 m (14,000 ft). Historically, chinchillas lived in an area that included parts of Bolivia, Peru and Chile, but today, colonies in the wild are known only in Chile. Along with their relatives, viscachas, they make up the family Chinchillidae. They are also related to the chinchilla rat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Chinchilla_lanigera_%28Wroclaw_zoo%29-2.JPG/330px-Chinchilla_lanigera_%28Wroclaw_zoo%29-2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinchilla"},{"title":"Chinchilla (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Daisy Bertenshaw, also known as Chinchilla, is a British singer and rapper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/CHINCHILLA_-_Close_Up_-_Tallinn_Sona_Festival_Grounds_-_GerliToomingPhoto.jpg/330px-CHINCHILLA_-_Close_Up_-_Tallinn_Sona_Festival_Grounds_-_GerliToomingPhoto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinchilla_(singer)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Habitat_du_Chinchilla_lanigera_-_Auco.jpg/500px-Habitat_du_Chinchilla_lanigera_-_Auco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Habitat_du_C